25:## Priced gap / cures (for the practice-job re-attempt)
26:- **Timing 55 — primary cure (convergent with motion):** the performance ends at ~8.5 s inside the 14 s specimen window, leaving a long final idle hold; per-char cadence and line pauses are not stretched to the sung phrase lengths. Cure: price per-line durations from the window (e.g. line-level start offsets / slower charMs + longer linePauseMs summing to ~14 s), not a single global cadence.
27:- **Motion 83 + timing (convergent defect, Amendment A1 rule):** the cursor DOM node is rebuilt every animation frame, so its CSS blink clock restarts and blinking does not read during holds. Cure: persistent cursor element; update only the text node.
28:- **Reusability 78:** config covers the specimen family, but robust multilingual reuse (combining characters, RTL scripts, very many/long lines) still requires logic changes — slice-by-code-point typing and a max-visible-lines scroll/trim policy are the named cures.
29:- **Readability 80:** layout shifts as new lines appear and long content can exceed screen height. Cure: reserve final layout (wrapped heights + cursor space) before typing so revealed characters occupy stable positions.
30:- Gap to bar: average needs +5.8 with timing lifted ≥70; the timing cure alone (55→~80) would add ~+5 to the average, so the freeze risk sits in timing + the cursor cure, not in purity.
33:First five-lens wave for this item (no prior T03 attempt; no cross-wave delta). T15's filed average (78.5) was a FOUR-lens instrument — deltas across that boundary are labeled as different instruments per Amendment A5.4 and are not compared here.
