65:## What moved, and the reusability regression (recorded for the next attempt)
66:- Timing 55→78 and motion 83→92: the bundled timing + persistent-cursor cures landed; timing's return prices the remaining gap as the schedule being an allocation model rather than vocal-anchored evidence (unresolved source timing — the packet carries no timed transcript), not a failed mechanism.
67:- Reusability 78→68 — regression with priced causes in the return, all verified against the source by the seat: (1) the header comment documents a `?charMs=` override the code never parses — a documentation/code mismatch introduced this attempt; (2) `maxVisibleLines` trims only past lines — future lines' slots (prompt + reserved height) are all displayed from the start, so the policy does not cap the visible window for many-line configs; (3) fallback pause arithmetic has no overflow guard — with many lines, start offsets can run past the window while the typing budget clamps to zero; (4) RTL layout remains unimplemented (deferred in the governing plan; the return prices it as a standing reusability cap, as the plan's WHY scaffold anticipated). These are the head of the next attempt's cure list.
