16:Arithmetic (seat-recomputed from the filed SCORE lines): 76+82+100+76+82 = 416; average 83.2; minimum 76. Bar: average ≥85 AND minimum ≥70.
19:Priced cures (lenses <85):
20:- motion 76 (<85): the plate pan wraps by 120 px every ~6.67 s without matching repeated geometry — visible jumps, plus a reset at the cycle boundary. Cure: seamless tiled landscape (repeat period = pan wrap) on a continuous pan clock that does not reset at cycle wrap. CONVERGENT with T137 motion and T135 motion — the shared engine's primary cure.
21:- timing 82 (<85): the lens finds no 80 ms dwell in the segment table against the packet's 80 ms floor claim — the floor dwells stand in the film outside this segment window; priced for attempt 2 as a table audit against onset-table rows 8–57 (any sub-120 ms dwell found there enters the table verbatim).
22:- reusability 76 (<85): swap semantics for the dwell table are harness-side (onsets recomputed outside buildTimeline in the probe); cure: move onset derivation into the engine (CONFIG carries words + dwells; onsets derived) so a table swap is CONFIG-only end to end.
23:- readability 82 (<85): red #e63329 on sky #a9c6d4 ≈ 2.4:1 contrast leaves thin margin at 80–160 ms dwells. Cure priced with the convergent contrast cure below.
24:CONVERGENT-LENS RULE: background-motion defect (motion on T132/T135/T137 — tiled-pan cure for the RSVP family; T137's own cure is a still plate, see RUN §9.1) and red-on-pale contrast (readability on T132/T134/T135) are the wave's two convergent defects; both lead attempt 2.
