45:**Delta vs attempt 1: 90.8 − 83.2 = +7.6 (signed).** Per-lens deltas: motion 76→96 (+20) · timing 82→100 (+18) · purity 100→100 (0) · reusability 76→78 (+2) · readability 82→80 (−2). Score attribution: BUNDLED (staged checkpoints isolate construction, not score movement).
47:Cure outcomes (from the filed returns):
48:- C1 seamless tiled pan + continuous clock + sun un-panned: MOVED — motion return credits tile closure and total-elapsed pan verbatim ("Each tile closes at its opening height… ridges advance from total elapsed time through every word cut, the blank beat, and the text loop"), motion +20.
49:- C2 darkened red #b91f16: PARTIALLY — readability return computes 3.58:1 vs sky but prices the far ridge behind the lower glyphs at 3.12:1 and prescribes a darker red (≥4.5:1 against all plate colours) for a future attempt; readability −2 despite the sky-contrast cure landing as computed.
50:- C3 derived onsets + dwellScale: MOVED on schedule claims (timing 100; reusability credits CONFIG-only table swaps) but reusability's residual findings cap its movement at +2.
51:- C4 swap semantics + validation + overflow: PARTIALLY — the final dwell plays in full (both motion and timing returns credit 13920–14040); validation is priced incomplete by reusability: rejection does not stop page startup (a rejected build still touches the DOM and a zero tile period would loop), mode contracts lack value-shape checks (derived word shapes, bands zero WPM, countdown array lengths, dwells rounding to zero).
52:- C5 table audit + R1 correction: MOVED — timing 100, no re-pricing of the absent 80 ms dwell; the return verifies the filed reconciliation.
53:- C6 typed transition: MOVED — motion and timing both price the 160 ms as an accounted beat, not a hole.
54:- C7/C8/C9 geometry / fit / contracts: PARTIALLY — canvas and fit are consumed and credited; reusability prices one unresolved resize case (a word impossible at the live stage width displays at the minimum size instead of a defined overflow response; countdown scaling applies after fitting).
57:Firing history note (A-C003-1): the first firing wave's motion and reusability sessions were terminated (SIGTERM, parallel load) with no return produced, and its timing/purity/readability returns were written to /tmp and LOST when /tmp was wiped before the content-copy step — that material is recorded UNAVAILABLE (their observed tails are not filed as scores). All five lenses were re-fired once, sequentially, with -o destinations under the workspace; the re-fired returns above are the governing preserved returns, sha-verified at filing, each with a session read-scope receipt in codex/attempt-2/.
