32:- **Motion 83 (minimum lens):** (1) the tail pair runs two simultaneous per-word fronts where the film runs one continuous front across `is spoken.` (D11) — cure: drive the pair with one spatial front across the intervening space. (2) The first chunk cut clips the last 18 ms of `uses`' fill + its settle — priced against the film's own cut (L2 stands mounted at 41.500 while `uses` is still in speech), so the cure is a boundary-frame verification of the outgoing state at each cut, not an assumed hold. (3) Label/chunk handoff: 80 ms same-position overlap (label at ≈36% opacity at first mount) — verify against source boundary frames and match the observed handoff.
