    19	### Motion census (A10.3) — frames extracted by the builder, viewed firsthand
    20	1 s spacing across the window (run dir census-t244/, copied to artifact census/): f-73.5 df78f3f6… · f-74.5 98996d90… · f-75.5 1643dbb0… · f-76.5 fbf2ad22… · f-77.5 69f64afd… · f-78.5 32ecccc3… · f-79.5 3b022088… · f-80.5 f6bec07a… · f-81.5 32570c11… (full SHA-256 in artifact census listing + build-record). Fine pass at 0.25 s across L4 onset: g-79.75 3f2dfd1c… · g-80.00 ecf0450f… · g-80.25 2191ae46… · g-80.75 0926f053… · g-81.00 7526e816… · g-81.25 d6a2cce7….
    21	
    22	### Mechanics + sub-beats (firsthand from census frames + evidence frames)
    23	1. **Fixed bottom band:** the caption line sits at ~86% of frame height, horizontally centred, one line at a time, on the black field below the diagram. No band box/background — text directly on black.
    24	2. **Two-state word colour:** unspoken words render dim grey; spoken words render full white. Pixel probe (PIL, band crop y 0.82–0.92 of frame): f-74.5 bright columns max 224–242 vs dim columns max 71–101; f-77.5 (line complete) all columns 194–201; f-80.5 bright 112–122 at the reading-order head vs dim 43. Dim ≈ 40% of full brightness.
    25	3. **Reading-order sweep (RTL):** the text is Persian, reading order right→left. f-74.5: rightmost two words («اون شب») white, remainder dim. ev/066 (~66 s): right portion white, left dim. g-80.25→f-80.5: the line's reading-order head is white first. The bright region is always a reading-order PREFIX of the line — spoken words stay white; the highlight never jumps or lights a suffix.
    26	4. **Word-granular stepping:** between census instants the bright prefix grows word by word (no letter-level gradient observed at 0.25 s spacing; the current word appears to flip/brighten at its onset — transition shorter than 250 ms, bounded not settled).
    27	5. **Line lifecycle:** a line appears at its speech onset (all dim except the first word brightening), sweeps to fully white at its last word, holds fully-lit briefly (f-77.5: L2 fully white 0.5 s after its ASR end, before L3's chunk dominates), and is replaced by the next line at the next onset. One line owns the band at a time (Owner Cure 2 phase exclusivity applies by analogy).
    28	6. **Diagram independence:** the diagram above animates on its own schedule; the band mechanic is independent of it — the recreation builds the BAND only (diagram is specimen content, not the technique; §8 split: band mechanic first).
    29	
    30	### Variables (§1.3 extraction)
    31	Line texts + word segmentation · per-line onset/end · per-word onset allocation · dim colour · spoken (bright) colour · word brighten transition duration · line hold-after-complete · band vertical position · font size/stack/weight · stage aspect (9:16 vertical) · total duration. Every variable becomes a CONFIG key (§2 table).
    32	
    33	### Schedule basis (A7)
    34	**segment-anchored** — line onsets/ends sit at their ASR-measured source times, re-based to segment t=0 by CONFIG segmentStartMs (73500). Per-word onsets inside a line are an **allocation**: proportional to word character length across the line's measured interval (ASR carries no word-level timings; the allocation is named here and in CONFIG derivation code, never presented as measured).
    35	
