## Priced cures (for Condense / a future attempt; none blocks the PASS)
- **Motion 83 (minimum lens):** (1) the tail pair runs two simultaneous per-word fronts where the film runs one continuous front across `is spoken.` (D11) — cure: drive the pair with one spatial front across the intervening space. (2) The first chunk cut clips the last 18 ms of `uses`' fill + its settle — priced against the film's own cut (L2 stands mounted at 41.500 while `uses` is still in speech), so the cure is a boundary-frame verification of the outgoing state at each cut, not an assumed hold. (3) Label/chunk handoff: 80 ms same-position overlap (label at ≈36% opacity at first mount) — verify against source boundary frames and match the observed handoff.
- **Timing 86:** the `is` settle envelope (easeOutCubic over 120 ms) predicts ≈70% recovery at 46.750 s vs ≈85% in the micro-census centroid sample — cure: fit the settle curve to that sample and recheck SF6/SF7. The derived windows for `so`/`are` stand tile-capped at 80/90 ms with source fidelity unverified (no census front measured for either) — carried as bounded derivations.
- **Reusability 86:** (1) expose the settle easing as CONFIG and make fittedFontPx measure with the same wordSpaceEm gaps the renderer uses (the fit currently measures space-joined text). (2) Letter segmentation differs between state (UTF-16 length) and DOM (code-point iteration) — unify before any supplementary-plane replacement text. (3) Finding 3's concrete instance is REBUTTED with the mechanical receipt: `are` derives vOn = source 43420 (43300 + 120, segment-rel 3920) and tile-caps to vEnd = source 43510 (rel 4010), duration **+90 ms** — the return's 43,540 start double-counts the lag; a full schedule dump verifies all 17 windows have positive durations (builder-run, this close). The underlying class — validate mixed measured/derived schedules after capping, with an explicit rule for intentional measured overlap (the D11 tail pair) — is carried as a named cure regardless.
- **Readability 88:** cap height clears the ~11 px floor by 0.12 px on the Liberation instrument (full ink height 15.00 px) — verify span geometry in the actual browser font at 360 px when a browser is available; the label-overlap cure is shared with motion (3).
- No convergent-lens defect (Amendment A1): no single defect is named by two lenses except the label handoff (motion + readability) — it stands as the first cure above.
